title: mf log contexts
tags: [[CLI command]] [[Event log]]
kind: reference
summary: List the log contexts with their counts and what undid them, newest first, reading no operation

```
> log context 12  2026-11-15 14:02  field add tag:string=jazz  (10000 operations)  [undoes log context 9]   ← HEAD
  log context 9   2026-11-15 13:40  field add tag:string=blue  (10000 operations)  [undone]
```

One line per log context, newest first: its own operations, how many log contexts are nested in it, and
what an undo says — `[undone]` or `[partly undone]` on a log context that was undone, `[undoes
log context N]` on the undo. `--in LABEL` lists the log contexts nested in one (the units of work
otherwise), `--limit N` and `--all` bound the list. Unlike [[mf log list]], no operation is
read, so a write to ten thousand records costs one line ([[Log context summaries]]); `mf log show`
goes into one log context.
